# LineageOS dependencies for the mt6877 platform.
#
# HONEST STATE: this tree is NOT buildable yet and this file does not pretend
# otherwise. Every entry below is a REAL, EXISTING repository, because an
# invented dependency fails `breakfast` and CI while hiding the actual gap.
#
# What exists and is listed, versus what does not and is named in README.md.

# --- hardware: MediaTek (real, used for the SoC HALs) ----------------------
android_hardware_mediatek
android_device_mediatek_sepolicy_vndr

# --- hardware: AISP / MTK media (real, needed for camera/audio on MTK) ----
# Listed for reference. A porting device only inherits this if it wires in
# MediaTek's camera/audio stack rather than AOSP's.
hardware_mediatek

# --- device: this repository ------------------------------------------------
# (the mt6877 platform tree itself)

# --- vendor -----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT LISTED, because it does not exist: vendor_mediatek_mt6877-common
# must be created. This is one of the two real walls -- see README.md.

# --- kernel -----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT LISTED, and cannot be. The device runs kernel 4.19.191+ and realme
# published no 4.19 device tree (their kernel-4.19 directory has 4 files and
# zero .dts). So there is no kernel repo to depend on; the platform ships a
# PREBUILT kernel instead (TARGET_PREBUILT_KERNEL in BoardConfigCommon.mk).
#
# The 6.6 tree DOES exist and DOES compile, but the device does not run it.
# If the device is ever updated to A15, this dependency becomes:
#   kernel_mediatek_mt6877-common-6.6
# and the prebuilt goes away. Worth knowing before investing in A13-era work.